=Write the Reel/Short script and shot list for this car article's short-form vertical video.

ARTICLE TITLE (AR): {{ $json.draftHeadline }}
SOURCE: {{ $json.source }}
CONTENT BEATS (same content beats used for the carousel — one object per genuine fact/claim/comparison this article supports): {{ JSON.stringify($json.draftCarouselSlides) }}
SOURCE CITATIONS: {{ JSON.stringify($json.draftSourceCitations) }}

Arabic text must be Arabic script (never Franco/Arabizi). Base every beat only on the content beats given above — do not invent specs or claims. If one of the content beats has slide_role "con", give it a real beat near the end rather than skipping it.

parameters.jsCode:
const draft = $json; // Parse Reel Script's output: Parse AI Draft fields + reelScript* fields

// Distinct PostId so this row/page/Telegram approval never collides with the Carousel post's
// own row for the same source article - matching-by-PostId is how the Sheet update, the
// Telegram YES/NO reply lookup, and the Notion "Post Id" filter all identify a row/page.
const reelPostId = String(draft.postId || '') + '-reel';

const beats = draft.reelScriptBeats || [];
const shotListText = beats.length
  ? beats.map(b =>
      `Beat ${b.beatNumber} (${b.durationSeconds}s)\nShot: ${b.visualDirection}\nOn-screen (AR): ${b.onScreenTextAr}\nVO (AR): ${b.voAr}\nTone: ${b.voTone}`
    ).join('\n\n')
  : 'No beats generated - reel script generation failed for this article (see reelScriptSource).';

// Cross-branch read, same convention as Merge Slides Into Item / Send Telegram Approval
// reaching into a sibling branch by node name: Build Video Scenes -> Call Media Render Video
// -> Set Video Output is a parallel branch off the same Parse AI Draft fan-out, not upstream
// of this node, so $json itself never carries videoUrl.
let videoUrl = null;
try { videoUrl = $('Set Video Output').item.json.videoUrl || null; } catch (e) { /* video branch didn't run in this execution */ }

return [{
  json: {
    ...draft,
    postId: reelPostId,
    format: 'Reel',
    videoUrl,
    // No per-slide PNGs exist for a script-only Reel row - reuse the hero image as the one
    // visual so the Sheet's ImageURLs column and Notion's Image files property aren't empty.
    renderedImageUrls: draft.imageUrl ? [draft.imageUrl] : [],
    reelShotListText: shotListText,
  },
}];

